<worksheet xml:id="LinearAlgebraExamEPage3" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title> Linear Algebra Sample Exam E - PAGE 3 </title>
    

<page>
      <p>  5. (2 points) Write down the solutions to <m>A\vec{x} = \vec{b}</m> in parametric vector form. You do not need to show your work.  
      </p>

      <p align="center">
        <me>A = \begin{pmatrix} 1 &amp; -2 &amp; 0 &amp; 0 &amp; 1 \\ 0 &amp; 0 &amp; 1 &amp; 0 &amp; 2 \\ 0 &amp; 0 &amp; 0 &amp; 1 &amp; -4 \end{pmatrix}, \quad \vec{b} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 4 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}</me>
      </p>

      <p>
  <m>\rule{0pt}{5cm}</m> 
      </p>

      <p>  6. (2 points) Please show your work for this question.  
      </p>
      <p>
        Construct a linear system and use row reductions to determine <m>a, b, c</m> so that the function <m>y = a\cos(2\pi t) + b\sin(2\pi t) + c</m> passes through the points <m>P(0, 5)</m>, <m>Q\left(\frac{1}{4}, 2\right)</m>, <m>R\left(\frac{1}{2}, 1\right)</m>. Please show your work.
      </p>
</page>

  
  
</worksheet>